I cannot construct the requested two-step consensus-interaction network with the available Human Protein Atlas tools. The tool set exposes gene/protein annotation, expression, subcellular localization, pathology, and protein-class data, but **does not provide the HPA consensus-interaction edge table or an export of the HPA master gene table**. Therefore I cannot validly:

- enumerate, filter, deduplicate, or make undirected consensus-interaction edges;
- restrict interaction endpoints to the atlas master-table universe;
- calculate first-/second-layer sizes, seed degrees, shared-neighbour counts, or intermediary path counts;
- identify/rank the requested twelve second-layer genes;
- draw the requested network-derived heatmaps or ranked bar chart.

The seed identifiers and HPA drug-target classification that *are* available are:

| Seed | Ensembl gene ID | FDA-approved drug target in HPA protein class |
|---|---|---|
| EGFR | ENSG00000146648 | Yes |
| ERBB2 | ENSG00000141736 | Yes |
| MET | ENSG00000105976 | Yes |

No interaction-derived values or gene lists are reported because calculating them from search-result annotations rather than the specified HPA consensus interaction dataset would not meet the requested definition.

